<title>BELGIUM: Finland's Niinisto unsure about German gold plan.</title>
<headline>Finland's Niinisto unsure about German gold plan.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Finance Minister Sauli Niinisto said on Wednesday it was unclear whether a revaluation of gold reserves, which Germany is considering, could be accepted as a way to reduce the budget deficit.</p>
<p>Niinisto said he was not sure whether a revaluation of Bundesbank gold reserves would be aimed at reducing the deficit or the debt level as part of efforts to meet the criteria for monetary union.</p>
<p>If it was intended for the debt level, Niinisto told Reuters he did not have much problem with the plan as the European Commission had earlier said member states could sell gold for that purpose.</p>
<p>But if such a measure was designed to help reduce the deficit, Niinisto added, &quot;it is not at all clear that one could accept that kind of manoeuvre. I think there is a question mark if they are talking about deficits.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
